0,Trans–New Guinea languages,https://grokipedia.com/page/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea is perhaps the third-largest language family in the world by number of languages. The core of the family is considered to be established, but its boundaries and overall membership are uncertain. The languages are spoken by around 3 million people.",Amam,Trans-New Guinea
1,Trans-New-Guinea languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/trans-new-guinea-languages/,"The Trans-New Guinea language group includes about 400 languages. By virtue of the number of speakers and the number of languages, it is the largest group of non Austronesian Papuan languages.",Amam,Trans-New Guinea
