7,"Trans-New Guinea - Wiktionary, the free dictionary",https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Trans-New_Guinea,"3 The Ndom language belongs to the Trans-New Guinea family. It is spoken by about 1200 people on the isle of Kolopom (Pulau Kolepom, Pulau Kimaam or Pulau Dolok, formerly Frederick Hendrik Island) off the coast of the Indonesian half of New Guinea.",Amam,Trans-New Guinea
